      "content": "TRANSFER INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "df7b6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36); font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "09796f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0b796f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Students must earn a \"C\" grade or higher in all courses required in the major. All students who are offered admission to the university are admitted as Pre-Economics majors. Students must complete ECON 1A, ECON 1B, MATH 24, and STAT 1 with a \"C\" or better, have an overall 2.0 GPA, and be in good standing to declare the major. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Business Administration, the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Business Administration 2.0, and the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Economics are compatible with the B.A. in Economics at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. The MATH 24 requirement may also be met by completing MATH 26A or MATH 30. Students planning ahead for graduate work in Economics should consult an advisor regarding additional and/or focused coursework in mathematics, statistics, and computer science. For additional information, please visit: Department of Economics .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students must earn a \"C\" grade or higher in all courses required in the major.</span></li><li><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">All students who are offered admission to the university are admitted as Pre-Economics majors. Students must complete ECON 1A, ECON 1B, MATH 24, and STAT 1 with a \"C\" or better, have an overall 2.0 GPA, and be in good standing to declare the major.</strong></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Business Administration, the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Business Administration 2.0, and the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Economics are compatible with the B.A. in Economics at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The MATH 24 requirement may also be met by completing MATH 26A or MATH 30.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students planning ahead for graduate work in Economics should consult an advisor regarding additional and/or focused coursework in mathematics, statistics, and computer science.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/social-sciences-interdisciplinary-studies/economics/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of Economics</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
